    "pressure": {
      "file": "dynamic_balancing_machine_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Two correction planes cancel static and couple unbalance",
      "description": "An unbalanced rotor's heavy spot creates a rotating centrifugal force F = m·e·ω², which shakes the soft pedestals at once per revolution. The pick-ups measure amplitude; the photo-cell gives the phase, so the console calculates the correction mass and angle for each of two planes (dynamic unbalance = static + couple). Residual unbalance is checked against the required grade, e.g. ISO 21940-11 G6.3 for fans and pump impellers or G2.5 for turbine rotors: U_per = G·m / ω (g·mm).",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
